<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chama Cha Mapinduzi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CCM, Party of the Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chama Cha Mapinduzi (CCM), the Party of the Revolution, is the ruling party of Tanzania, formed on 5 February 1977 by the merger of the mainland's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-african-national-union">Tanganyika African National Union</a> and Zanzibar's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afro-shirazi-party">Afro-Shirazi Party</a>. It was the sole legal party until 1992 and has won every national election since multi-party politics began, making it one of the longest-ruling parties in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chama-cha-mapinduzi.jpg" alt="Chama Cha Mapinduzi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SVG: amygdalicGloss Logo: CCM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Chama_Cha_Mapinduzi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
